ws in 1349.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_al-Hasan_Ali_ibn_Othman"},{"name":"Abu Inan's conquest of the central Maghreb","from":1352,"to":1358,"outcome":"Marinid gains that did not last: Bejaia 1353, Tunis August 1357, abandoned the same year; Abu Inan strangled on 10 January 1358.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Inan_Faris"},{"name":"Abu Faris's campaigns","from":1401,"to":1431,"outcome":"Hafsid gains: Tripoli 1401, Gafsa 1401, Biskra 1402, Tozeur 1404, Algiers 1410-1411; the Zayyanid sultan beaten in 1424 and replaced in 1431.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafsid_dynasty"},{"name":"Spanish conquests of Bejaia and Tripoli","from":1509,"to":1510,"outcome":"Spanish victory: Bejaia taken in 1509 and Tripoli in 1510.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regency_of_Algiers"},{"name":"Hafsid and Kuku war against Algiers","from":1520,"to":1525,"outcome":"The Hafsids and Kuku take Algiers in 1520; Hayreddin retakes it in 1525.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regency_of_Algiers"},{"name":"Ottoman-Habsburg struggle for Tunis","from":1534,"to":1574,"outcome":"Barbarossa takes Tunis 16 August 1534; Charles V retakes it 21 July 1535 and restores Muley Hasan as a Spanish client; the Ottomans retake it in 1569, Don Juan of Austria in 1573, the Ottomans finally in 1574.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_Tunis_(1535)"}],"certainty":[{"from":1229,"to":1574,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty line is given on any page; the Saharan edge and the Tripolitanian and Algerian frontiers are approximate throughout."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafsid_dynasty","title":"Hafsid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regency_of_Algiers","title":"Regency of Algiers"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Tripoli_(1551)","title":"Siege of Tripoli (1551)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beylik_of_Constantine","title":"Beylik of Constantine"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_Tunis_(1535)","title":"